From b704fd62be95014e48019a268a00cb8b18a11860 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:14:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 193/194] glm_moe_dsa: prompt [q_a | kv_a] and indexer queries
 on their row owners (TF_GLM_PROMPT_OWNER_PROJ, default off)

The two-halves prompt path computed every row's replicated [q_a | kv_a] (2624 x 6144 block FP8) on every rank,
right after the ffn exchange had summed each row on one owner. TF_GLM_PROMPT_OWNER_PROJ (a mask, read at each chunk
through dsa_block.ownerPolicy):
- 1 (fused): inside the ffn exchange, each row owner norms its summed residual rows with the next layer's input
  norm and projects them (dsa_block.ownerRows), and the compact rows ride the residual all-gather in one NCCL group
  (in place into a per-half room); the next mixer takes them as proj_done.
- 2 (separate): the owners project from the main stream's normed rows after the exchange, then one all-gather on
  the main stream (the simple form, to price the fusion).
- 4 (qb): the indexer's wq_b only for the query rows this rank selects (sparse.splitRows, dsaSelect's own rule,
  TF_GLM_INDEX_SPLIT); index keys are still written by every rank.
The rooms sit in the gathered buffer past both halves' exchange spans (ownRoom; host test for every chunk length at
TP3-TP8): no new memory. Layer 0, the KV-split path and whole (non-halves) chunks keep the replicated projection.

Exact: qmmf's K slices come from the shape alone, so a row's sums do not depend on the call's row count.
tf-cuda-test glm-owner-proj (real EXL3-K4 layers 6, 40, 41; R 4096/2048/1088/961/1984/1857/300; TP4 owners):
105 byte comparisons equal ([q_a | kv_a] fused and separate, q_norm, kv_norm rows, split qb rows, DSA picks and
counts), and a flipped byte and a one-row shift are caught at every shape. test-glm-owner-proj-host: switch parse,
split rows, rooms.

Idea: Codex's (OpenAI) analysis docs/gpt-sol-new.md section 5.1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UQVvNktFCvQrvpNUbqtqBX
